[{"category":"section","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat","page":"Home","text":"The RegularlySampledFormat package provides an interface for working with RSF files.\n\nThe RSF file format is used in the Madagascar open-source package for geophysical data analysis.\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.Datapath-Tuple{}","page":"Home","text":"Datapath() -> String\n\nReturn the path to the data directory. The path is determined by checking the following sources in order of priority:\n1. The environment variable `DATAPATH`.\n2. A file named `.datapath` in the current working directory.\n3. A file named `.datapath` in the user's home directory.\n4. If none of the above sources provide a path, the function defaults to returning\nthe current working directory (`\"./\"`).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.Datapath"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.Temp-Tuple{}","page":"Home","text":"Temp() -> (String, IO)\n\nCreate a temporary data path. The temporary data path is determined by checking the following sources in order of priority:\n1. The environment variable `TMPDATAPATH`.\n2. The result of `Datapath()` function.\n\nReturns a tuple containing the path to the temporary file and an IO object for writing to the file.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.Temp"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.add!-Tuple{SimTab, String}","page":"Home","text":"add!(t, keyval)\n\nEnter a key-value pair into the symbolic table `t` from a string of the form \"key=val\".\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.add!"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.enter!-Tuple{SimTab, String, String}","page":"Home","text":"enter!(t, key, val)\n\nEnter a key-value pair into the symbolic table `t`.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.enter!"},{"category":"function","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getbool","page":"Home","text":"getbool(key, default)\n\nExtract a boolean parameter from the parameter table `par` for a given `key`. \nIf the key is not found, return the `default` value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getbool"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getbool-Tuple{SimTab, String}","page":"Home","text":"getbool(t, key)\n\nExtract a boolean parameter from the symbolic table `t` for a given `key`.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getbool"},{"category":"function","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getbools","page":"Home","text":"getbools(key, n, default)\n\nExtract an array of boolean parameters from the parameter table `par` for a given `key`. \nThe array will have length `n`. If the number of values in the table is less than `n`, the last value will be repeated to fill the array. If the number of values is greater than `n`, only the first `n` values will be returned. If the key is not found, return the `default` value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getbools"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getbools-Tuple{SimTab, String, Int64}","page":"Home","text":"getbools(t, key, n)\n\nExtract an array of boolean parameters from the symbolic table `t` for a given `key`. \nThe array will have length `n`. If the number of values in the table is less than `n`, the last value will be repeated to fill the array. If the number of values is greater than `n`, only the first `n` values will be returned.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getbools"},{"category":"function","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getfloat","page":"Home","text":"getfloat(key, default)\n\nExtract a float parameter from the parameter table `par` for a given `key`. \nIf the key is not found, return the `default` value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getfloat"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getfloat-Tuple{SimTab, String}","page":"Home","text":"getfloat(t, key)\n\nExtract a float parameter from the symbolic table `t` for a given `key`.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getfloat"},{"category":"function","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getfloats","page":"Home","text":"getfloats(key, n, default)\n\nExtract an array of float parameters from the parameter table `par` for a given `key`. \nThe array will have length `n`. If the number of values in the table is less than `n`, the last value will be repeated to fill the array. If the number of values is greater than `n`, only the first `n` values will be returned. If the key is not found, return the `default` value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getfloats"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getfloats-Tuple{SimTab, String, Int64}","page":"Home","text":"getfloats(t, key, n)\n\nExtract an array of float parameters from the symbolic table `t` for a given `key`. \nThe array will have length `n`. If the number of values in the table is less than `n`, the last value will be repeated to fill the array. If the number of values is greater than `n`, only the first `n` values will be returned.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getfloats"},{"category":"function","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getint","page":"Home","text":"getint(key, default)\n\nExtract an integer parameter from the parameter table `par` for a given `key`. \nIf the key is not found, return the `default` value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getint"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getint-Tuple{SimTab, String}","page":"Home","text":"getint(t, key)\n\nExtract an integer parameter from the symbolic table `t` for a given `key`.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getint"},{"category":"function","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getints","page":"Home","text":"getints(key, n, default)\n\nExtract an array of integer parameters from the parameter table `par` for a given `key`. \nThe array will have length `n`. If the number of values in the table is less than `n`, the last value will be repeated to fill the array. If the number of values is greater than `n`, only the first `n` values will be returned. If the key is not found, return the `default` value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getints"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getints-Tuple{SimTab, String, Int64}","page":"Home","text":"getints(t, key, n)\n\nExtract an array of integer parameters from the symbolic table `t` for a given `key`. \nThe array will have length `n`. If the number of values in the table is less than `n`, the last value will be repeated to fill the array. If the number of values is greater than `n`, only the first `n` values will be returned.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getints"},{"category":"function","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getpar","page":"Home","text":"getpar(p, key, T, default)\n\nExtract a parameter of type `T` from the parameter table `p` for a given `key`. \nIf the key is not found, return the `default` value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getpar"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getpar-Tuple{SimTab, String, DataType}","page":"Home","text":"add!(t, keyval)\n\nEnter a key-value pair into the symbolic table `t` from a string of the form \"key=val\".\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getpar"},{"category":"function","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getpars","page":"Home","text":"getpars(p, key, n, T, default)\n\nExtract an array of parameters of type `T` from the parameter table `p` for a given `key`. \nThe array will have length `n`. If the number of values in the table is less than `n`, the last value will be repeated to fill the array. If the number of values is greater than `n`, only the first `n` values will be returned. If the key is not found, return the `default` value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getpars"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getpars-Tuple{SimTab, String, Int64, DataType}","page":"Home","text":"getpars(t, key, n, T)\n\nExtract an array of parameters from the symbolic table `t` for a given `key`. \nThe array will have length `n` and will be of type `T`. If the number of values in the table is less than `n`, the last value will be repeated to fill the array. If the number of values is greater than `n`, only the first `n` values will be returned.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getpars"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getprog-Tuple{Par}","page":"Home","text":"getprog(p)\n\nExtract the program name from the parameter table `p`.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getprog"},{"category":"function","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getstring","page":"Home","text":"getstring(key, default)\n\nExtract a string parameter from the parameter table `par` for a given `key`. \nIf the key is not found, return the `default` value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getstring"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.getstring-Tuple{SimTab, String}","page":"Home","text":"getstring(t, key)\n\nExtract a string parameter from the symbolic table `t` for a given `key`.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.getstring"},{"category":"function","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.input!","page":"Home","text":"input!(t, filep)\n\nInput key-value pairs into the symbolic table `t` from a file stream `filep`.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.input!"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.output-Tuple{SimTab, IOStream}","page":"Home","text":"output(t, filep)\n\nOutput the contents of the symbolic table `t` to a file stream `filep`.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.output"},{"category":"method","location":"#RegularlySampledFormat.string!-Tuple{SimTab, String}","page":"Home","text":"string!(t, string)\n\nEnter key-value pairs into the symbolic table `t` from a string of the form \"key1=val1 key2=val2 ...\".\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RegularlySampledFormat.string!"}]
